cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SDPX.jl in academic work, please cite it as below."
title: "SDPX.jl: a native Julia solver for high-precision conic optimization"
abstract: >-
  SDPX.jl is a native Julia solver for linear, second-order cone, and
  semidefinite programs. It uses primal-dual interior-point methods and
  supports Float64, BigFloat, and MultiFloats arithmetic,
  structured sparse and dense KKT paths, original-coordinate certificates,
  and MathOptInterface/JuMP integration. It is a substantial rewrite of
  SDPJSolver.jl and is motivated by the S-matrix/EFT, modular, and lattice
  bootstrap programs.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Yongjun
    family-names: Xu
    email: yongjunx23@gmail.com
version: 0.6.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/yongjunx23-del/SDPX.jl"
keywords:
  - conic optimization
  - linear programming
  - second-order cone programming
  - semidefinite programming
  - interior-point method
  - arbitrary precision
  - S-matrix bootstrap
  - modular bootstrap
  - lattice bootstrap
  - Julia
references:
